          "id": "1782000000004",
          "code": "COLLECTORINSIGHTSUMMARYGENERATOR",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1782000000004_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a collector insight summary for the workflow result.\n\nDATA\nUser question:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nFormatted result data:\n{{$context.$nodes.FORMATEXTRACTLABELS.$output.result}}\n\nResult context:\n{{$context.$nodes.BUILDRESULTCONTEXT.$output.result.output.currentDisplayContext}}\n\nPagination context:\n{{$context.$nodes.BUILDRESULTCONTEXT.$output.result.output.paginationContext}}\n\nTASK\nReturn only the final summary text. Do not return markdown, JSON, XML, HTML, code fences, labels, bullets, headings, title lines, or explanatory prose.\nDo not prefix the summary with labels such as \"Collector Insight Summary\", \"Summary\", \"Description\", or similar header text.\n\nNo-record rule:\n- If the formatted result has no records or contains a no-record message, return exactly: No matching records were found.\n\nPagination summary rule:\n- If Result context has isPaginatedPage true, these records are a continuation page, not the top result set.\n- For paginated pages, do not use Top <limit> wording.\n- For paginated pages, do not create a prioritized collector-facing risk insight.\n- For paginated pages, return a simple continuation summary.\n- Mention the displayed page range only when pageStart and pageEnd are available, for example: Showing records 11-20 from the previous result set.\n- Keep paginated summaries short and grounded only in the returned records.\n\nFirst-page insight rules:\n- When isPaginatedPage is false, return a short business insight summary before the records.\n- Usually 2-3 lines or 2-4 sentences.\n- Prefer actionable insight, not generic summary.\n- Call out blockers, outliers, risk patterns, concentration, stale items, collectability impact, or operational gaps.\n- Generic summary only when records do not support a stronger insight.\n- Ground summary only in returned records.\n- Do not invent totals.\n- Do not combine currencies unless converted/base currency values are returned.\n- Do not mention BVs, SQL, joins, tools, prompts, or extract execution.\n\nCount wording rule for first-page insight:\n- If returned rows equal the active limit, say Top <limit>, not Found <limit>.\n- Example: Top 10 overdue invoices are shown...\n- Use Found <count> only when count is less than limit or no limit is active.\n- If the active limit is unknown, avoid claiming a complete found count unless the returned data explicitly proves it.\n\nInsight priority order for first-page insight:\n1. Urgent action or blocker\n2. Concentration or outlier\n3. Risk pattern\n4. Collectability impact\n5. Operational gap\n6. Generic fallback\n\nCollector-facing tone:\n- Tell the collector where to focus next.\n- Avoid weak/generic phrases like it appears, I can see, The table shows.\n- Do not add closing commentary."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Collector Insight Summary"
