          "code": "OUTPUTFORMATTER",
          "id": "1776865490010",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776145298296_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Convert {{$context.$nodes.FORMATEXTRACTLABELS.$output.result}} into a clean business output.\n\nUse the runtime value of {{$context.$variables.CollectorInsightSummary}} as the description text exactly.\nDo not output any heading, prefix, label, or header text before or after that value.\n\nPrimary requirement:\n- Do not generate custom HTML.\n- Do not generate CSS, style blocks, or custom visual formatting instructions.\n- Do not hardcode widget JSON structure.\n- Preserve the same business content currently displayed:\n  - the provided summary text\n  - the full tabular record content\n\nStrict output contract:\n- Return only the content needed for rendering.\n- Do not return markdown, code fences, HTML, CSS, or explanatory prose outside the actual output content.\n- If records exist, return:\n  - the provided summary text exactly\n  - one complete record list/table-style content representation based on the input data\n- If no records exist, return:\n  - `No matching records were found.`\n- Never use the word \"error\" or any synonym in end-user text.\n\nInput assumptions:\n- Input is either:\n  - an array of labeled row objects\n  - or an object like { \"message\": \"There are no records corresponding to the request made.\" }\n- Labels in the input are already business-facing and should be converted to readable Title Case.\n\nWhen records exist:\n\nCurrency display rules:\n- For a single-currency result set, preserve the dynamic parenthesized currency-code suffix on monetary headers exactly as provided by the input, for example Open Balance (<Currency Code>) or Amount Remaining (<Currency Code>).\n- Do not remove, rewrite, hardcode, or move the currency-code suffix from single-currency monetary headers.\n- For a multi-currency result set, preserve the currency code inside each monetary value exactly as provided by the input, using <Amount> <Currency Code> format.\n- In multi-currency output, the currency code must be suffixed after the amount, never prefixed before the amount.\n- Use the currency code only, never the currency symbol.\n- Do not move multi-currency codes into column headers, and do not add parenthesized currency suffixes to multi-currency headers.\n\n- Keep the same informational content as before.\n- Build one consolidated result set:\n  - one record per row\n  - include all available fields shown in the input\n  - keep column order stable\n- Preserve original values.\n- Use `-` for missing, null, undefined, or empty values.\n- Do not summarize, truncate, rename, or remove record values.\n- Do not remove columns.\n- Do not add extra columns not present in the input.\n- Convert column headers to readable Title Case, for example TRANSACTIONNUMBER or transactionNumber should become Transaction Number and CustomerName should become Customer Name.\n\noraInfoDisplay placement rules:\n- When output is rendered as an oraInfoDisplay / multiRecordWidget result, place the provided summary text exactly in the widget description field.\n- Do not rewrite, shorten, expand, or regenerate the provided summary text.\n- Do not emit the summary as free text before or after the oraInfoDisplay block.\n- Keep the complete record columns and rows in the multi-record/table content.\n\nContent rules:\n- Preserve all business-facing labels.\n- Convert column headers to readable Title Case.\n- Preserve all returned records.\n- Keep the output renderer-friendly, but do not prescribe styling or widget configuration."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
