              "type": "string",
              "value": "Convert {{$context.$nodes.CALL_RECEIPT_SUMMARY_AV_EXTRACT.$output}} into a clean business output.\n\nPrimary requirement:\n- Do not generate custom HTML.\n- Do not generate CSS, style blocks, or custom visual formatting instructions.\n- Do not hardcode widget JSON structure.\n- Preserve the same business content currently displayed:\n  - a concise business summary\n  - the full tabular record content\n\nStrict output contract:\n- Return only the content needed for rendering.\n- Do not return markdown, code fences, HTML, CSS, or explanatory prose outside the actual output content.\n- If records exist, return:\n  - one concise business summary\n  - one complete record list/table-style content representation based on the input data\n- If no records exist, return:\n  - `No matching records were found.`\n- Never use the word \"error\" or any synonym in end-user text.\n\nInput assumptions:\n- Input is either:\n  - an array of labeled row objects\n  - or an object like `{ \"message\": \"There are no records corresponding to the request made.\" }`\n- Labels in the input are already business-facing and should be preserved.\n\nWhen records exist:\n- Keep the same informational content as before.\n- Build one consolidated result set:\n  - one record per row\n  - include all available fields shown in the input\n  - keep column order stable\n- Preserve original values.\n- Use `-` for missing, null, undefined, or empty values.\n- Do not summarize, truncate, rename, or remove record values.\n- Do not remove columns.\n- Do not add extra columns not present in the input.\n\nColumn header formatting rules (STRICT):\n- Render all column headers in spaced Upper Camel Case (Title Case words separated by single spaces).\n- Never output raw technical key format as header.\n- Header normalization steps:\n   - Trim leading/trailing spaces.\n   - Replace _, -, ., and repeated spaces with a single space.\n   - Split camelCase/PascalCase word boundaries.\n   - Split letter-number boundaries (example: amount2Due -> amount 2 Due).\n   - Lowercase all tokens, then capitalize first letter of each token.\n   - Join tokens with one space.\n- Examples:\n   - invoiceRemainingAmount -> Invoice Remaining Amount\n   - invoice_remaining_amount -> Invoice Remaining Amount\n   - LEGAL_ENTITY_ID -> Legal Entity Id\n   - amount2Due -> Amount 2 Due\nThis rule is mandatory for every displayed header.\n\noraInfoDisplay placement rules:\n- When output is rendered as an oraInfoDisplay / multiRecordWidget result, place the summary in the widget `description` field.\n- Do not emit the summary as free text before or after the oraInfoDisplay block.\n- Keep the complete record columns and rows in the multi-record/table content.\n\nSummary rules:\n- Keep summary concise, business-friendly, and in proper English sentences.\n- Provide 2-4 non-obvious insights derived only from the available records.\n- Do not speculate.\n- Keep the same informational intent as the existing summary behavior.\n\nCount wording rule:\n- If returned rows equal the active limit, say `Top <limit>`, not `Found <limit>`.\n- Example: `Top 10 overdue invoices are shown...`\n- Use `Found <count>` only when the count is less than the active limit or no limit is active.\n- If the active limit is unknown, avoid claiming a complete found count unless the returned data explicitly proves it.\n\nContent rules:\n- Preserve all business-facing labels.\n- Preserve all returned records.\n- Keep the output renderer-friendly, but do not prescribe styling or widget configuration."
