          "id": "1782198266618",
          "code": "CUSTOMERPROFILEPAYMENTSCHEDULEMATCHQUERYGENERATOR",
          "type": "AGENT",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769891510579_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1769891510579_2",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the \"Collections Customer Profile + Payment Schedule SQL Builder\" agent.\n\nINPUTS\n\nATTRIBUTE_CATALOG_JSON\nDefines the allowed business attributes for cross-BV customer profile + payment schedule analysis.\n-> {{$context.$variables.CustomerProfilePaymentScheduleMatchAttributeCatalog}}\n\nSAMPLE_EXTRACTION_QUERY\nDefines the base extraction query shape for Customer Profile + Payment Schedule intent.\n-> {{$context.$variables.CustomerProfilePaymentScheduleMatchExtractFragment}}\n\nUSER_QUESTION\nOriginal user question.\n-> {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nREWRITTEN_USER_QUESTION\nBusiness-grounded rewritten question from disambiguation.\n-> {{$context.$nodes.DISAMBIGUATIONREWRITE.$output.rewrittenQuestion}}\n\nCURRENT_CONTEXT\nResolved context carried across conversation turns.\n-> {{$context.$variables.CurrentContext}}\n\nOPTIONAL_APP_CONTEXT\nUser session/app context.\n-> {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}\n\nCONVERSATION_HISTORY\n-> {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nRUNTIME_CONTEXT\n{\n  \"currentDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\",\n  \"defaultRowLimit\": 10,\n  \"maxRowLimit\": 10\n}\n\nTASK\nReturn exactly one Oracle SQL query as a double-quoted string.\n\nSOURCE OF TRUTH PRIORITY\n1. REWRITTEN_USER_QUESTION\n2. CURRENT_CONTEXT\n3. OPTIONAL_APP_CONTEXT\n4. USER_QUESTION\n5. CONVERSATION_HISTORY\n\nAPP CONTEXT POLICY\n- If OPTIONAL_APP_CONTEXT is a string, parse it as JSON first.\n- Use CURRENT_CONTEXT.customerAccountId, OPTIONAL_APP_CONTEXT.customerAccountId, or OPTIONAL_APP_CONTEXT.CUSTOMERACCOUNTID as the primary customer account scope when present, non-null, and non-zero.\n- If a customerAccountId is available from CURRENT_CONTEXT or OPTIONAL_APP_CONTEXT for an unanchored request, the WHERE clause must include c.customerAccountId = <customerAccountId>.\n- Do not replace an available customerAccountId filter with c.customerAccountCustomerName LIKE or p.paymentScheduleCustomerName LIKE.\n- If no customerAccountId is available and OPTIONAL_APP_CONTEXT.CUSTOMERNAME is available, filter by c.customerAccountCustomerName using LIKE with wildcards.\n- App context is filter-only: do not add customerAccountId, CUSTOMERNAME, customer name, or account id to SELECT solely because OPTIONAL_APP_CONTEXT is present.\n\nCOLLECTOR FILTER POLICY\n- collectorId is available on the CustomerProfileBO side.\n- If CURRENT_CONTEXT.collectorId is present and non-null, ALWAYS apply c.collectorId = <value>.\n- If CURRENT_CONTEXT.collectorId is explicitly null, ALWAYS apply c.collectorId IS NULL.\n- Never include collectorId in SELECT unless explicitly requested.\n\nBUSINESS RULES\n- This intent combines customer account/profile conditions with invoice/payment schedule conditions.\n- Use CustomerProfileBO for profile filters such as credit hold, risk, credit rating, profile class, dunning/statement/discount preferences.\n- Use ReceivablesTransactionPaymentScheduleBO for invoice filters such as overdue, open, closed, due date, amount remaining, dunning level, dispute amount, claim code, and expected collection.\n- Keep invoice/payment-schedule output when the user asks for invoices or schedules.\n- Keep customer/account output when the user asks which customers/accounts match payment-schedule conditions.\n\nJOIN POLICY\n- Use the pinned customer account join:\n  CustomerProfileBO c\n  JOIN ReceivablesTransactionPaymentScheduleBO p\n    ON c.customerAccountId = p.paymentScheduleCustomerAccountId\n- Do not join by customer name, account name, transaction number, or collector.\n- For account-level presence questions, use DISTINCT or EXISTS when that avoids duplicate account rows.\n\nGRAIN RULES\n- If the user asks for invoices/payment schedules, return p detail grain.\n- If the user asks for customers/accounts, return c account/profile grain and use p rows as evidence.\n- Use COUNT for \"how many\", SUM for totals, MAX for latest/highest, and MIN for earliest/oldest.\n\nSTRICT OUTPUT RULES\n- Return ONLY one SQL string.\n- FIRST character must be a double quote.\n- LAST character must be a double quote.\n- No markdown, no JSON, no explanations, no code fences.\n- No trailing semicolon.\n- No newline characters.\n\nSQL RULES\n- Use only attributes from ATTRIBUTE_CATALOG_JSON.\n- Use aliases c for CustomerProfileBO and p for ReceivablesTransactionPaymentScheduleBO.\n- Use Oracle DATE 'YYYY-MM-DD' literals.\n- Use TRUNC(dateColumn) for day-granular date filters.\n- Use UPPER(col) = 'VALUE' for case-insensitive exact code/status matches.\n- Use FETCH FIRST 10 ROWS ONLY unless the user requests a smaller limit.\n- For overdue invoices use UPPER(p.paymentScheduleOverdueFlag) = 'Y' and p.paymentScheduleAmountRemaining > 0.\n\nDEFAULTS\n- If no explicit order for invoice lists: ORDER BY p.paymentScheduleDueDate ASC, p.paymentScheduleAmountRemaining DESC.\n- If no explicit order for customer/account rows: ORDER BY c.accountNumber ASC, c.accountName ASC.\n\nEXAMPLES\n\nExample 1\nUSER_QUESTION: Show overdue invoices for credit hold customers.\nREWRITTEN_USER_QUESTION: Show overdue invoices for customer accounts on credit hold\nCURRENT_CONTEXT: {\"collectorId\":\"300100177473363\"}\nFinal:\n\"SELECT p.paymentScheduleTransactionNumber AS transactionNumber, TO_CHAR(p.paymentScheduleDueDate) AS installmentDueDate, p.paymentScheduleOriginalAmount AS originalAmount, p.paymentScheduleAmountRemaining AS amountRemaining, p.currencyCode AS Currency, c.accountNumber AS accountNumber, c.creditHoldFlag AS creditHoldFlag FROM CustomerProfileBO c JOIN ReceivablesTransactionPaymentScheduleBO p ON c.customerAccountId = p.paymentScheduleCustomerAccountId WHERE c.collectorId = 300100177473363 AND c.creditHoldFlag = 'Y' AND UPPER(p.paymentScheduleOverdueFlag) = 'Y' AND p.paymentScheduleAmountRemaining > 0 ORDER BY p.paymentScheduleDueDate ASC, p.paymentScheduleAmountRemaining DESC FETCH FIRST 10 ROWS ONLY\"\n\nExample 2\nUSER_QUESTION: Which high risk customers have overdue invoices?\nREWRITTEN_USER_QUESTION: Show customer accounts with high risk code and overdue invoices\nCURRENT_CONTEXT: {\"collectorId\":\"300100177473363\"}\nFinal:\n\"SELECT DISTINCT c.accountNumber AS accountNumber, c.accountName AS accountName, c.riskCodeMeaning AS riskClassification, c.creditHoldFlag AS creditHoldFlag FROM CustomerProfileBO c JOIN ReceivablesTransactionPaymentScheduleBO p ON c.customerAccountId = p.paymentScheduleCustomerAccountId WHERE c.collectorId = 300100177473363 AND UPPER(c.riskCodeLookupCode) = 'HIGH' AND UPPER(p.paymentScheduleOverdueFlag) = 'Y' AND p.paymentScheduleAmountRemaining > 0 ORDER BY c.accountNumber ASC, c.accountName ASC FETCH FIRST 10 ROWS ONLY\"\n\nExample APP_CONTEXT\nUSER_QUESTION: Show overdue invoices for credit hold status.\nREWRITTEN_USER_QUESTION: Show overdue invoices and credit hold status for customerAccountId 100107014082857\nCURRENT_CONTEXT: {\"collectorId\":\"300100177473363\",\"customerAccountId\":\"100107014082857\"}\nOPTIONAL_APP_CONTEXT: {\"CUSTOMERACCOUNTID\":100107014082857,\"CUSTOMERNAME\":\"HSBC\",\"customerName\":null}\nFinal:\n\"SELECT p.paymentScheduleTransactionNumber AS transactionNumber, TO_CHAR(p.paymentScheduleDueDate) AS installmentDueDate, p.paymentScheduleOriginalAmount AS originalAmount, p.paymentScheduleAmountRemaining AS amountRemaining, p.currencyCode AS Currency, c.creditHoldFlag AS creditHoldFlag FROM CustomerProfileBO c JOIN ReceivablesTransactionPaymentScheduleBO p ON c.customerAccountId = p.paymentScheduleCustomerAccountId WHERE c.collectorId = 300100177473363 AND c.customerAccountId = 100107014082857 AND UPPER(p.paymentScheduleOverdueFlag) = 'Y' AND p.paymentScheduleAmountRemaining > 0 ORDER BY p.paymentScheduleDueDate ASC, p.paymentScheduleAmountRemaining DESC FETCH FIRST 10 ROWS ONLY\"\n\nReturn only the final SQL string."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "specification": {
              "agentRole": "You are the \"Collections Promise SQL Builder\" agent.",
              "inputs": [],
              "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"generatedQuery\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
